---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Affiliate Disclosure | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.name} uses affiliate links, and the rules it holds itself to.`}
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="body-sm">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>

      <h2>What an affiliate link is</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to accommodation, tours, clothing and gear are affiliate links. If you book or
        buy through one, this site may earn a commission. It never changes the price you pay.
      </p>

      <h2>How they are marked</h2>
      <p>
        Every affiliate link on this site opens in a new tab and carries a
        <code>sponsored</code> attribute, which is the machine-readable way of declaring the
        commercial relationship. Where a stay log or gear note contains one, it is stated on the
        page as well.
      </p>

      <h2>The rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Nothing is recommended that has not actually been used, stayed in, or worn.</li>
        <li>A commission never buys a positive review. The pros and cons are what they are.</li>
        <li>Destinations are never sponsored. Where a trip was paid for by someone else, it is said so on the page.</li>
        <li>Nothing is listed because it pays. The commission follows the recommendation, never the other way round.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
